{
 "annotations": {
  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "Revenue breakdown by dimension"
 },
 "description": "`get_breakdown` compares `channel`, `entry_page`, and `visitor_history` rows for the requested period and the preceding equal-length window (or compare_start_date/compare_end_date). Each row reports current values plus previous values and deltas where comparable. Channel attribution_model supports last_touch, first_touch, linear, and time_decay. Ad spend is grouped through `ad_channel_mapping` (site-specific rows override global rows), and candidate revenue is summed from matching last_touch session channels regardless of attribution_model. Candidate values are context only; they are not paid attribution and no Paid Attribution ROAS is calculated. Unattributed purchase revenue appears as a separate row and is excluded from attributed totals. `entry_page` uses dashboard_entry_page_summary_window; country/device filters are unsupported there. `visitor_history` uses the dashboard's visitor-type history rule. `revenue_status='unconfirmed'` means available signals do not confirm revenue history: monetary fields and monetary deltas are null, while session counts remain numeric; it does not prove purchase measurement is unconfigured. Internal retrieval failures return `isError=true`, `revenue_status='error'`, and `revenue:null`. `is_demo` is independent of revenue_status. Comparisons are available only when the preceding window has observed trend data, no preceding-window fetch error occurred, and the first non-bot, non-dwell-only session's site-calendar date is on or before the preceding window's start date. `page` and `entry_page` default to at most 20 rows and report omitted counts. `filter.channel` drills into campaign rows. site_id is optional when OAuth-authenticated. Default period is 30 days; accepted values are today, 7d, 30d, 90d, or 1-365. Explicit start_date/end_date are inclusive calendar dates in the site's analysis timezone. Spend uses inclusive JST dates from `ad_spend_daily.date`; trend and session windows use site timezone. Country (ISO2) and device filters apply where the source RPC supports them; unsupported axes are called out in notes.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
